From dd2bd2f7783f0c887f558a72b16e82e156fdb69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 04:38:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add ToolStripControlHost (host an arbitrary control on a
 strip)

ToolStripControlHost was absent - a compile break for any custom hosted
ToolStrip item and any type reference to it. Implement it as a ToolStripItem
that embeds a hosted Control's GTK widget into the tool item and forwards the
common item members (text, size, enabled, font, colours) to the control, with
Focus/Select and the OnSubscribe/OnUnsubscribeControlEvents hooks subclasses
override to bridge events. Dispose detaches the hosted widget before the base
item tears down its own, so disposing the host does not destroy a widget the
control still owns.

Covered by ToolStripControlHostFunctionalTests (null guard, Control property,
named ctor, text/enabled/font forwarding, the subscribe/unsubscribe hooks on
construct/dispose, and adding a host to a strip).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
